id: snatch
name: Snatch
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
special: true
usageLimit: 1/round
clashSkill: thievery
clashDefenderSkills: perception, thievery
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Clash of your Thievery against the Perception or Thievery of an Opponent in your Melee Range: win, and the Basic
  Item you named is yours.
text: >
  Snatch Maneuver [1/Round]: Take something being held by your opponent!
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent within your Melee Range who you know possesses a certain Basic Item. Make a Skill Clash
  (Thievery vs Perception/Thievery). If you win, you take that Basic Item from that Opponent.

---

# Opened by 2+ Ranks in Thievery, like every other Skill's. Which Basic Item is named before the Clash, from theirs
# (use-maneuver.mjs askSnatch); won, it is taken as Pickpocket takes one (chat.mjs settlePickpocket).
